Steps:
1. Go to https://download.unity3d.com/download_unity/5f63fdee6d95/LinuxEditorInstaller/Unity-2022.3.60f1.tar.xz
2. Find your Bopl folder and copy the contents of the files of this repository into your Bopl folder, as well as the Unity archive
3. Run install.sh and it will patch the game
4. Go to the gear icon in Steam > Properties > Advanced Launch Options and use: ./BoplBattle.x86_64 #%command%
5. Play!

This does not contain any assets from Bopl Battle; it only provides patches to a few DLLs that are open source.

Online works;
I wasted WAY too much time patching Facepunch.Steamworks.Win64.dll without realizing that Facepunch.Steamworks is open source and I can just download the Linux build and rename it to a Windows build.
The version I found that works was Facepunch.Steamworks v2.3.2; also used libsteam_api.so which is also shipped with the DLL in the Unity folder. I had to rename this to libsteam_api64.so for some reason.

Interestingly I needed something called libBCrypt.so too; Unity crashes without "BCryptGenRandom" from this library
I """""learned""""" C and implemented it myself
Source:
#include <sys/random.h>
#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>

int BCryptGenRandom(
    void *_algorithm,
    uint8_t *pbBuffer,
    uint32_t cbBuffer,
    uint32_t _flags)
{
    getrandom(pbBuffer,(size_t)cbBuffer,0);
    return 0;
}

(The C purists might kill me for this one)
(Actually they might not I don't know if they will)

A MacOS build is definitely possible but I don't have a Mac to test, so...
Maybe if someone asks I'll try my best!
